@clawsweeper re-review

Both remaining findings are repaired in 4f1648a28173. The existing capture session now holds immutable synchronous and asynchronous claims per maintenance scope. Legacy finalization synchronously settles legacy partial responses and writes, releases their stores, and keeps later legacy calls inactive until explicit initialization; host async claims retain their existing awaited lifecycle cleanup. The final claim ends the shared session. Both initialization orders fail before repair and pass with real workers afterward, including reopening and eventual store release.

Gateway capture finalization now runs after media drains even when stopping media cleanup rejects, while shared database closure keeps its existing guard. That regression fails before repair; all 83 Gateway cases pass. The 181-case capture/runtime/maintenance/input/batching run passes, as do types, lint, cycles and line-cap checks. Fresh managed P0–P2 review is clean. The PR body and SDK docs describe the final behavior and retain exact-source update evidence.

@clawsweeper re-review

The reviewed compatibility and Gateway repairs are composed with main in 6a01cab02c31. Both capture and TUI worker contracts and both test inventories are retained; main's config-file routing assertions still cover the migrated OpenAI tests. The diagnostic-command selector moved into its existing reader owner to satisfy the line cap without changing admission or replies.

A real loopback regression also caught inherited RequestInit precedence: the server received an overriding POST/body/headers while capture preferred the original Request. The recorder now uses those overrides, and the regression passes. All 407 composed cases, the final 61 transport/reader/TUI/inventory cases, core/test/tooling types, lint, cycles, formatting and the exact staged line-cap check pass. A fresh complete two-pass managed P0–P2 review is clean. Older source-bound update receipts remain explicitly scoped in the PR body.
